-- title:
--   A Fricke automorphism of the level-N modular function field
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a non-zero natural number. Write $F_N^{\mathrm{full}} = \mathbb{Q}(\mathtt{divisorExpansions}\ N)$ for the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q)) =$ `LaurentSeries ℚ` generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the set `divisorExpansions N`, and let $F_N =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` be the intermediate field of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the image of $F_N^{\mathrm{full}}$ under the coefficientwise map `coeffEmb` induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The assertion is that there exists a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $F_N$ with the following property: for all non-zero natural numbers $a, b$ with $ab = N$, and for every element $x$ of $F_N$ whose underlying Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ equals the image under `coeffEmb` of `qExpand ℚ a jq`, the underlying Laurent series of $\sigma(x)$ equals the image under `coeffEmb` of `qExpand ℚ b jq`. Here `jq` is the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNumQ` over $\mathbb{Q}$, i.e. the $q$-expansion of $j$, and `qExpand ℚ a` is the ring homomorphism on Laurent series that multiplies all exponents by $a$, so that `qExpand ℚ a jq` is the expansion of $j(q^a)$. Thus $\sigma$ interchanges the expansions of $j(q^a)$ and $j(q^b)$ whenever $ab = N$.
--
--   This is the Fricke (Atkin–Lehner) involution $w_N$, $\tau \mapsto -1/(N\tau)$, realised algebraically as a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphism of the function field of $X_0(N)$ presented through $q$-expansions, together with the only property of it used downstream, namely that it exchanges $j(q^a)$ and $j(q^b)$ for $ab = N$. It feeds the construction of the Galois- and Hecke-equivariant pairings on the modular curve and the analysis of reduction of places modulo $\ell$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_frickeAlgEquiv_modularFunctionFieldBar.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open AlgebraicCurve ModularCurve

theorem ModularCurve.exists_frickeAlgEquiv_modularFunctionFieldBar (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] :
    ∃ σ : modularFunctionFieldBar N ≃ₐ[AlgebraicClosure ℚ] modularFunctionFieldBar N,
      ∀ (a b : ℕ) [NeZero a] [NeZero b], a * b = N →
        ∀ x : modularFunctionFieldBar N,
          (x : LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)) = coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (qExpand ℚ a jq) →
            ((σ x : modularFunctionFieldBar N) : LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))
              = coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (qExpand ℚ b jq) := by sorry
